# Dependency Injection with Koin

## Overview

This project uses **Koin** for dependency injection. All dependencies must be provided via Koin modules, never instantiated manually in production code.

Reference DI modules:
- [AppModule.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/dev/sonle/pdfscanner/core/di/AppModule.kt)
- [DatabaseModule.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/dev/sonle/pdfscanner/core/di/DatabaseModule.kt)
- [RepositoryModule.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/dev/sonle/pdfscanner/core/di/RepositoryModule.kt)
- [ScannerModule.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/dev/sonle/pdfscanner/core/di/ScannerModule.kt)

## General Rules

### 1. Never use manual instantiation in ViewModels
❌ **BAD**:
```kotlin
class MyViewModel : ViewModel() {
    private val useCase = MyUseCase()  // DON'T
}
```

✅ **GOOD**:
```kotlin
class MyViewModel(
    private val useCase: MyUseCase
) : ViewModel()
```

Register in Koin:
```kotlin
viewModelOf(::MyViewModel)
factoryOf(::MyUseCase)
```

### 2. Always use constructor injection
```kotlin
class MyRepositoryImpl(
    private val dao: MyDao
) : MyRepository
```

### 3. ViewModels in Compose
```kotlin
@Composable
fun MyScreen(viewModel: MyViewModel = koinViewModel()) { }
```

## Module structure

- `appModule` — use cases, ViewModels, app services
- `databaseModule` — Room database and DAOs
- `repositoryModule` — repository bindings
- `scannerModule` — document detection pipeline
- `dispatcherModule` — coroutine dispatchers

## Scoping

- `single { }` — singletons (database, repositories)
- `factory { }` / `factoryOf(::)` — use cases
- `viewModelOf(::)` — ViewModels

## Testing

Use `KoinTest` or manual Koin modules with mocks in unit tests. See [TestDispatcher.kt](mdc:app/src/test/java/dev/sonle/pdfscanner/TestDispatcher.kt).
